    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nFixes and enhances the `portal/query-requires-error-alert` ESLint rule to better detect valid query error-handling patterns (including `isError` usage in JSX props/conditionals), avoid cross-scope false matches, and improve reporting/documentation.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Adds scope-aware `isError` identifier resolution and member-expression tracking (e.g., `query.isError`) to determine which specific query is handled.\n- Expands accepted “error handled” patterns to include passing `isError` into certain JSX props (e.g., `isInvalid`, `errorMessage`) and recursively parses complex conditional expressions.\n- Updates plugin README with detailed, example-driven documentation of accepted patterns.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 2 out of 2 changed files in this pull request and generated 2 comments.\n\n| File | Description |\n| ---- | ----------- |\n| frontend/eslint-plugin-portal/src/rules/query-requires-error-alert.ts | Reworks query tracking + adds scope-aware detection and multi-location reporting for unhandled queries/mutations. |\n| frontend/eslint-plugin-portal/README.md | Documents valid error-handling patterns supported by the rule with concrete TSX examples. |\n\n\n\n",
